id: SEC-019
title: Server-Side Template Injection (CVE-2025-23211)
category: security
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .py .java .kt .php
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/ venv/ .venv/
patterns:
  - regex: render_template_string\(.*request
    message: "User input in render_template_string() — Jinja2 SSTI enables RCE"
  - regex: Template\(.*request\.
    message: "User input in Template constructor — SSTI enables arbitrary code execution"
  - regex: Environment.*from_string.*request
    message: "Jinja2 Environment.from_string with request data — SSTI RCE risk"
fix: Never pass user input directly into template strings. Use render_template() with separate template files.